t_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running it.\npytest isn't installed here, so I'll run the test cases directly:\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** Python stores `2.675` as a binary float that is really `2.67499999999999982\u2026`, so `round(x, 2)` rounds it down. `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit (`round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`), which isn't the \"half up\" rounding the docstring promises.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now takes the number as Python prints it (`repr(x)`, so `2.675` stays `2.675`), rounds that to cents with `Decimal` using `ROUND_HALF_UP`, and returns a float as before. `add_vat` calls `round_money`, so it gets the fix too.\n\n**Tests:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py` covering `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `2.674\u21922.67`, `-2.675\u2192-2.68` and `3\u21923.0`. pytest isn't installed here, so I haven't run that file through pytest. I ran the same cases with a direct Python call instead: all six pass, while the old `round()` gives `2.67 / 1.0 / 0.12 / -2.67` on the half cases. The existing `split` test still passes.\n\n**Behaviour change:** negative halves now round away from zero (`-2.675 \u2192 -2.68`). Before, they rounded toward zero in this case.\n\n**Not changed:** `split` still uses `int(total * 100)`, which cuts off the fraction instead of rounding and can be thrown off by the same float error. It wasn't part of this bug, so I left it alone.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 250995, "requests_cache_write": 10369, "requests_cost_usd": 0.148804, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2334, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp